.TH GXWI-TERMINAL 1 2026-10-19 "Peios gxwi-terminal 0.1.0"
.SH NAME
gxwi-terminal \- GXWI terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gxwi-terminal
.RI [ directory ]
.br
.B gxwi-terminal
.I program
.RI [ argument ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Opens a window on the GXWI desktop with a shell in it, on a pseudoterminal.
The shell is the one named by
.B SHELL
as an absolute path in the environment, or
.I /bin/sh
if none is named, and it is started in the home directory of whoever signed in.
.PP
Given one argument that is an absolute directory, the shell is started there instead.
Given anything else, the first argument is run in place of the shell and the rest are passed to it.
.PP
The terminal belongs to the program and not to the browser showing it: a page that is closed and opened again, or another device looking at the same session, is shown the terminal as it stands.
.PP
The window closes when the shell ends.
Closing the window hangs the terminal up on whatever is running in it.
.SH INPUT
Each browser page buffers at most 1 MiB of pending input and sends it in order
in 16 KiB chunks, waiting for each chunk to be written to the pseudoterminal.
The application separately limits queued input and input being written across
pages to 1 MiB. Each incoming websocket message and frame is limited to 1 MiB.
A write acknowledgment means that the pseudoterminal accepted the bytes,
not that the program finished processing them.
.PP
If the page buffer fills, typing pauses while output continues.
A paste larger than the remaining space is refused in full with a visible message.
.PP
A broken connection with pending input produces an interruption warning.
Unconfirmed input is not replayed after reconnection; some bytes might already
have reached the program, and application-side input might still be written.
Check the terminal before entering commands again.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+C
Copy what is selected.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+V, Shift+Insert
Paste.
.PP
The desktop's own chords are the desktop's while the keyboard is in the terminal.
.SH SECURITY
The child runs with the session account's authority and inherited session environment.
Closing the application window hangs up the terminal; this is different from disconnecting a browser.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The application session ended normally.
.TP
.B 1
A connection, initialization, or application error prevented normal operation.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B TERM
Set to
.I xterm-256color
for what is started.
.TP
.B GXWI_DISPLAY
Names the desktop.
It is left in the environment of what is started, so a program run from the terminal can open windows of its own.
.TP
.B HOME
Initial working directory when it exists; otherwise use the filesystem root.
.TP
.B SHELL
Absolute shell path; a missing or nonabsolute value selects /bin/sh.
.TP
.B COLORTERM
Set to truecolor for the child.
.SH NOTES
Runs within a GXWI session.
Its parent supplies the session descriptors and identity; launch it through the desktop.
.SH SEE ALSO
The Peios learn documentation.
